solution:
To solve the congruence $11n \equiv 7 \pmod{43}$, find the multiplicative inverse of $11$ modulo $43$.

The multiplicative inverse of $11$ modulo $43$ is the number $a$ such that $11a \equiv 1 \pmod{43}$.

Using the extended Euclidean algorithm to find $a$:
   \begin{align*}
   43 &= 3(11) + 10 \\
   11 &= 1(10) + 1 \\
   10 &= 10(1) + 0
   \end{align*}

Working backward:
   \begin{align*}
   1 &= 11 - 1(10) \\
   &= 11 - 1(43 - 3(11)) \\
   &= 4(11) - 1(43)
   \end{align*}

This implies that $4(11) \equiv 1 \pmod{43}$, so $a = 4$.

Multiply both sides of the congruence $11n \equiv 7 \pmod{43}$ by $4$:
   \begin{align*}
   4(11n) &\equiv 4(7) \pmod{43} \\
   n &\equiv 28 \pmod{43}
   \end{align*}

Therefore, the solution is:
   \[ \boxed{28} \]

