solution:
Given that the projection of $\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ onto $\mathbf{w}$ is $\begin{pmatrix} -9/10 \\ 3/10 \end{pmatrix}$, we can deduce that $\mathbf{w}$ is in the direction of $\begin{pmatrix} -9/10 \\ 3/10 \end{pmatrix}$. Therefore, a unit vector $\mathbf{u}$ in the direction of $\mathbf{w}$ is:
\[ \mathbf{u} = \begin{pmatrix} -3/ \sqrt{10} \\ 1/ \sqrt{10} \end{pmatrix} \]

The projection of $\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$ onto $\mathbf{w}$ is given by $(\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{u}) \mathbf{u}$:
\begin{align*}
\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{u} &= 4 \left( -\frac{3}{\sqrt{10}} \right) + 1 \left( \frac{1}{\sqrt{10}} \right) = -\frac{12}{\sqrt{10}} + \frac{1}{\sqrt{10}} = -\frac{11}{\sqrt{10}} \\
(\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{u}) \mathbf{u} &= \left( -\frac{11}{\sqrt{10}} \right) \begin{pmatrix} -3/ \sqrt{10} \\ 1/ \sqrt{10} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{33}{10} \\ -\frac{11}{10} \end{pmatrix}
\end{align*}

So, the projection of $\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$ onto $\mathbf{w}$ is:
\[ \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 33/10 \\ -11/10 \end{pmatrix}} \]

